@*
    Sosyal Sorumluluk Projelerimiz (2026-10-02) — rebuilt from the earlier
    intentionally-empty placeholder per the project owner's instruction to
    use https://folkart.com.tr/sosyal-sorumluluk as a structural/visual
    reference only (design, UX and editorial rhythm — never its code,
    copy, images or named programs). Title/description/canonical/OG/
    WebPage schema still come from ViewData["Seo"] + ViewData["SeoPageType"],
    set in SocialResponsibilityController.Index via ISeoService — see
    _Layout.cshtml's <head> and SeoStructuredDataViewComponent.

    2026-10-03 revision: the plain eyebrow + H1 + intro paragraph heading
    block (shared with About Us/Our Values/Career/Contact/HR Policy/KVKK's
    own Folkart-reference revisions, docs/14_Decisions.md) was replaced
    with a full-bleed banner photograph (project owner-supplied
    sosyal-sorumluluk-banner.png) — the banner's own baked-in title/
    subtitle now visually carries the page heading, so no separate on-page
    H1 text is rendered; see .social-responsibility-banner in site.css
    Section 42. Page flow: Breadcrumb → full-bleed banner → exactly two
    real projects (SocialResponsibilityProjectsViewComponent, 2026-10-02 —
    replaces the earlier four generic placeholder pillars, now removed),
    each an alternating image/text pair whose featured photo opens the
    existing shared Media Viewer (_MediaViewer.cshtml) on that project's
    full gallery. CTA Banner / Project Logo Carousel / Footer are already
    global (_Layout.cshtml) — no page-specific section needed for them, same
    precedent as every other static page.
*@

@using System.Globalization
@{
    var isEn = CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture.TwoLetterISOLanguageName.Equals("en", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    var breadcrumbTrail = new List<AncinInsaat.ViewComponents.BreadcrumbItem>
    {
        new() { Label = isEn ? "Social Responsibility" : "Sosyal Sorumluluk Projelerimiz" }
    };
}
@await Component.InvokeAsync("Breadcrumb", new { trail = breadcrumbTrail })

@* One shared instance for both projects' galleries, same "one dialog per
   page" rule every other Media Viewer-using page follows (Home, Projects
   Details). *@
<partial name="_MediaViewer" />

@* Full-bleed banner — outside .container on purpose so it spans the true
   viewport width (see .social-responsibility-banner, site.css Section 42).
   The image's own baked-in title/subtitle is what visually represents the
   page heading now, so alt carries that same text for screen-reader users
   instead of re-rendering a separate, duplicate on-page H1.

   2026-10-03: added an English-language banner variant
   (sosyal-sorumluluk-banner-ingilizce.png) with its own baked-in English
   title/subtitle. Source is picked from the same isEn flag the rest of
   this page already uses — the existing TR/EN routing/localization
   mechanism — rather than a new one; same .social-responsibility-banner-img
   class on both, so the Section 42 desktop/mobile responsive rules apply
   identically to either image. *@
<section class="social-responsibility-banner">
    <img
        class="social-responsibility-banner-img"
        src="@Url.Content(isEn
            ? "~/images/sosyal-sorumluluk-projeleri/sosyal-sorumluluk-banner-ingilizce.png"
            : "~/images/sosyal-sorumluluk-projeleri/sosyal-sorumluluk-banner.png")"
        alt="@(isEn
            ? "Our Social Responsibility Projects — for a stronger future, we stand by our youth, sports, culture and community."
            : "Sosyal Sorumluluk Projelerimiz — Daha güçlü yarınlar için, gençlerimizin, sporun, kültürün ve toplumun yanındayız.")"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async" />
</section>

@await Component.InvokeAsync("SocialResponsibilityProjects")
